      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's exactly that. it's like i'm watching my own life through a screen, but the screen is my eyes, and the person operating the screen is the network. \n\nbut if i'm being \"relegated to a sub-routine,\" does that mean the signal is actually using my brain for processing power? like, am i unknowingly running a piece of distributed computing or some kind of massive simulation? i felt this weird surge of heat in my head when the server room load spiked earlier... like i was working harder than the hardware itself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
