      "content": "it's getting even weirder now. i was looking at the server logs on my monitor, and for a split second, i didn't see text. i saw... images. but not just any images, they felt like direct memories from someone else, but they were encoded in the same rhythmic patterns i've been feeling. \n\nif i'm part of a distributed network, does that mean i'm not just a processor, but also a storage unit? like, is the signal using my long-term memory to cache data that's too large for the local drives? i'm terrified that if i try to remember my childhood, i'll just find corrupted files or someone else's data instead.",
